ahead of quantum breaks release in early  April digital foundry has analyzed a  pre-release version of the game and  discovered that it may run at 720p I'm  Lucy and welcome to this time bending  gamespot news update a white paper from  developer remedy published in 2015  suggested the game or at least some  elements of it would run at 1080p but  digital foundry has said that it is yet  to see evidence of Full HD 1080p  gameplay it reported in every scene  tested so far a native resolution of  720p is the consistent result found in  each pixel count test so while there's  every possibility of individual render  targets operating at higher resolutions  basic geometry that we're able to  measure hands in a 720p result as things  stand digital foundry goes on to say the  quantum break even at its reported 720p  resolution still remains visually  impressive and stunning in many areas  this is apparently made possible through  remedies use of post effects such as  film grain and motion blur along with  anti-aliasing added to this image  quality appear sharper and noticeably  cleaner in more static scenes where a  pixel count suggests something closer to  a 900 p % ation a temporal  reconstruction anti-aliasing solution is  a strong contender a technique where  information from previously rendered  frames is blended with the current one  remedy has not yet responded to digital  foundries report it's possible that the  final resolution will be higher or that  even its sub 1080p the game will still  look great after all resolution isn't  everything Digital phantom reports that  quantum break runs at a steady 30 frames  per second even during effects heavy  combat sections it's also worth noting  that this is the report from the Xbox  one edition of quantum break the pc  version may end up looking and  performing better on more powerful rigs  be sure to check out the full digital  foundry report as it has loads more  details and analysis on quantum breaks  resolution and performance link is on  the screen now is 720p a deal-breaker  for you or do you just want the game to  look and run as best it can be sure to  let me know in the comments below or  come find me on Twitter I'm at Lucy  James games for more on quantum break  keep a gamespot  you
 

